cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ze Theory: An Interpretive Framework for Z₂ Lattice Gauge Theory"
message: "If you use Ze in your research, please cite the paper."
type: article
authors:
  - given-names: Jaba
    family-names: Tqemaladze
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8651-7243"
    email: jaba@longevity.ge
repository-code: "https://github.com/djabbat/ze-theory"
year: 2026
month: 7
abstract: "Ze-theory offers an interpretive framework for Z₂ lattice gauge theory in the language of active agents minimizing existence time through prediction. The Hamiltonian coincides with the standard Z₂ gauge theory (Wegner 1971); novelty is in conceptual reframing. Numerical results confirm a critical point v*=1−ln2, a quantum phase transition at Γ≈1.0 (matching Pfeuty 1970), and Wilson loop confinement on the cubic lattice."
keywords:
  - Z₂ lattice gauge theory
  - Monte Carlo
  - quantum phase transition
  - free energy principle
  - agent-based interpretation
license: Apache-2.0
